<h2>Why the guest sounds quieter</h2>
<p>The host talks into a microphone they know, in a studio they know. The guest comes in on a different microphone, from a different room, and sometimes over a remote line. Every voice enters the episode at its own level.</p>
<p>Editing takes care of the episode as a whole: it makes sure the whole thing plays at a sensible level. The gap between the two people talking in it usually stays. At home that's annoying. In a car, with road noise, it means a hand on the knob.</p>

<h2>What the app does</h2>
<p>LevelCast listens to the episode as it plays and evens out the speakers as it goes: whoever speaks quietly comes up, whoever is loud is held back. Levelling runs on the phone. The producer's file doesn't change, and no audio is sent anywhere to level it.</p>

