<p>There are three strengths. <strong>Normal</strong> brings up the quiet speaker and holds back the loud one, and suits most podcasts. <strong>Strong</strong> is for big gaps or a noisy car. <strong>Off</strong> plays the audio as it arrived. You can <a href="{{ collections.byKey.listen[lang] }}">hear the difference in the demo</a>.</p>

<h2>Where the episodes come from</h2>
<p>Podcasts are published in an open feed, and the audio lives on the producer's server. The app finds shows through Apple's podcast directory, and also takes a feed address or an episode link you paste in by hand. The episode plays straight from the producer's server, and the download is counted there.</p>

<h2>Everything inside</h2>
<ul class="checks">
  <li><strong>Speaker levelling</strong> at normal or strong, plus a separate setting per show.</li>
  <li><strong>Intro skip.</strong> Finds where the music ends and the talking starts, and offers to skip ahead.</li>
  <li><strong>Pace matching.</strong> A slow speaker is sped up a little, a fast one slowed down.</li>
  <li><strong>Playback speed</strong> from <span dir="ltr">0.8×</span> to <span dir="ltr">3×</span>.</li>
  <li><strong>Capture a moment.</strong> Hold the back button on your steering wheel, or a button in the player, to keep what was just said along with a transcript. Moments wait in your library to send once you've stopped.</li>
  <li><strong>Live transcript</strong> shown like song lyrics, <strong>search inside an episode</strong>, and <strong>key points</strong> that quote sentences from the episode itself. Transcription uses iOS speech recognition, on devices that support the episode's language.</li>
  <li><strong>Links from the episode notes</strong>, gathered in one place.</li>
  <li><strong>A short automatic rewind</strong> after an interruption, so you don't miss the end of the sentence.</li>
  <li><strong>Downloads</strong>, manual, automatic and ahead of time, plus background refresh with a new-episode alert.</li>
  <li><strong>Sleep timer</strong> that fades out instead of cutting off mid-sentence.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What's free and what's in a subscription</h2>
<div class="tiers">
  <section class="tier">
    <h3>Free</h3>
    <p>Search and follow shows, strong levelling, a queue of up to three episodes, resume where you left off, manual download, intro skip, moment capture and episode links.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="tier">
    <h3>Pro</h3>
    <p>Per-show levelling, an unlimited queue, automatic and advance downloads, speeds above <span dir="ltr">1.5×</span>, pace matching, background refresh and alerts, and the sleep timer.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="tier tier--accent">
    <h3>Pro AI</h3>
    <p>Everything in Pro, plus live transcript, search inside an episode and key points.</p>
  </section>
</div>
<p class="note">Both paid plans will be sold monthly or yearly through Apple, and the price is shown on the purchase screen before you pay.</p>

<h2>Privacy</h2>
<p>No account and no sign-up. Your library, queue, moments and settings stay on your phone. The app talks to Apple for search, and to the producer's server for the feed and the audio. The one exception is transcription on a device without on-device speech recognition for the episode's language: there iOS sends the clip to Apple's service, never to us. The full details are in the <a href="{{ collections.byKey.privacy[lang] }}">privacy policy</a>.</p>

<h2>Which devices</h2>
<p>iPhone with iOS 17 or later. The interface is in Hebrew and English.</p>
